.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt AMARCHY 1
.Os UP-Term
.Sh NAME
.Nm Amarchy ,
.Nm amarchy-menu ,
.Nm amarchy-gui ,
.Nm amnotify
.Nd Super-key shortcuts for the whole Amiga
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Amarchy
.Op Cm CX_PRIORITY Ar n
.Nm amarchy-menu
.Cm menu Ar node
.Nm amarchy-menu
.Cm viewer
.Nm amarchy-gui
.Cm menu Ar node
.Nm amarchy-gui
.Cm viewer
.Nm amnotify
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Ar title
.Op Ar body
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a commodity, listed in Exchange as AMARCHY, that binds the Left Amiga key
(called Super) plus a letter, digit or function key to an action: a menu
command or slash command of an UP-Term window, a new tab, a program to
start.
Install starts it at every boot from a block in S:User-Startup.
Only the keys of the key file are taken; every other Left Amiga key goes to
the program as before.
Left Amiga + M, Left Amiga + N, Left Amiga + the
mouse are never bound, and a press with Right Amiga down is never taken, so the
reset keys (Ctrl and both Amigas) stay safe.
Left Amiga + Alt is not used: Intuition makes it the left mouse button.
While an UP-Term window is active it matches the keys itself and
.Nm
leaves them alone.
.Pp
.Nm amarchy-menu
is the program the keys start:
Left Amiga + Space runs
.Ql amarchy-menu menu root ,
a short list filtered by typing,
and Left Amiga + K runs
.Ql amarchy-menu viewer ,
the list of every key.
.Nm amarchy-gui
is the drawn version of the same two screens: its own borderless window with
an icon in front of each row.
The setting
.Ql menu-style = graphical ,
.Ql menu-style = text
or
.Ql menu-style = minimal
in
.Pa ENVARC:up-term/up-term
(before the first section; default graphical) chooses which program Left Amiga
+ Space and Left Amiga + K start. No shipped chord starts the other one; bind
.Ql othermenu:root
or
.Ql otherviewer
in the keymap to get it (not with Alt: Left Amiga + Alt is the left mouse button).
.Ql minimal
starts
.Nm amarchy-gui
as plain text rows: no border, no icons, two colours (the fg and bg settings,
else the screen's own pens), a group row ends in
.Ql \ > .
The setting
.Ql amarchy-app-icons = generic ,
.Ql amiga
or
.Ql none
chooses the icons of app rows.
The icons come from a table made when the kit is built (dist/menu-icons in
the source), so a row of
.Pa keymap.user
cannot name an icon.
Window placement keys: Super plus Ctrl plus Shift plus an arrow key snaps the focused window to a half
of the screen, Super plus Ctrl plus Shift plus 1, 2, 3 or 4 to a quarter (top left, top right, bottom left,
bottom right) and Super plus Ctrl plus Shift plus C to the centre. Super plus an arrow key moves focus to the
neighbouring window. Super plus Ctrl plus Shift plus H, J, K or L swaps the focused tile with its neighbour,
and Super plus Ctrl plus Shift plus T floats or tiles the focused window (AmTile FLOAT TOGGLE).
Super plus Left and Right no longer switch tabs; Super plus comma and period still do.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ENVARC:up-term/keymap
The shipped key file (a copy is in ENV:up-term/keymap, read first).
Every Install replaces it; a different old file is first saved as keymap.bak.
.It Pa ENVARC:up-term/keymap.user
Your own rows; it survives a reboot and an upgrade.
Amarchy watches the ENV: copies, so an edit here applies after
.Ql Copy ENVARC:up-term/keymap.user ENV:up-term/keymap.user
or after a reboot; the ARexx command
.Ql RELOAD
rereads the files at once.
A row replaces the row for the same key;
.Ql super+t = none
unbinds one.
.It Pa UP-Term:Amarchy/Themes/NAME.theme
The shipped GUI themes of the drawn menu (the Omarchy colour themes; the default is tokyo-night).
.It Pa ENVARC:Amarchy/themes/NAME.theme
Your own GUI themes; a file of the same name as a shipped one wins.
To add one, copy an Omarchy
.Pa colors.toml
(keys accent, background, foreground, dark_foreground, optional mode = "light") to this drawer under the new name,
then pick it under Style > Theme in the menu or in the Menu theme row of UP-Term Prefs (Amarchy page).
It applies the next time the menu opens.
An unknown or unreadable theme name draws the compiled-in tokyo-night.
The terminal's own colours (Terminal theme, super+shift+t) are separate.
.El
.Pp
Each row reads
.Dl super[+shift][+ctrl][+rshift]+KEY = action ; label | category
Actions are menu:id, viewer, tab:new, tab:close, tab:next, tab:prev,
tab:goto N, menuid:NAME, slash:/command, run:command, open:uterm,
rexx:script, cap:kind and win:verb [argument]. The verbs are cycle, front, back, zip,
fullwidth, fullscreen, save, restore, move, size, focus, closedrawers, screen
and title.
Lines starting with a semicolon are comments.
.Sh ARexx
The port AMARCHY takes STATUS (hits, rows, enabled and active), RELOAD (read
the key files again), RUN
.Ar n
(do row n of the table), SHOW (the key viewer) and QUIT.
.Dl rx \(dqaddress AMARCHY RELOAD\(dq
.Pp
The command BAR takes STATUS, ON, OFF and TOGGLE and answers
.Ql bar=N draws=N panels=N launches=N raises=N ticks=N ;
OFF closes the status bar and its timer (the one second tick keeps running), ON opens it again.
STATUS answers the counters of the rest
.Ql ( ticks=N
ends it).
.Pp
The action
.Cm cap:screen ,
.Cm cap:window
and
.Cm cap:region
save a screenshot of the front screen, the active window or a dragged region as an IFF ILBM file in RAM:Shots
and put it on the clipboard.
.Sh NOTICES
A notice is a short message from Amarchy.
The port AMARCHY.NOTIFY takes
.Cm NOTIFY Ar title|body|seconds
(body and seconds may be left out; a literal | is written \\|; seconds 0 stays until dismissed),
.Cm COUNT
(notices shown now) and
.Cm CLEAR
(remove them all).
The command NOTES on the port AMARCHY answers the counts and the title of the last notice; STATUS ends with
.Ql shots=N notes=N .
.Pp
.Nm amnotify
sends one from a script.
The title is required;
.Ar seconds
is 0 to 3600.
Return code 0 means sent, 5 Amarchy is not running, 10 bad arguments.
.Dl amnotify -t 3 Done \(dqbuild ok\(dq
.Pp
.Pa UP-Term:S/safe-off
is the script behind System > Safe to switch off (Left Amiga + Esc opens that menu).
It runs
.Ql Reboot DRYRUN ,
which writes every volume out and restarts nothing, then posts the notice
.Dq Safe to switch off ,
or
.Dq Not all disks answered
with the output of Reboot as its body.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr UPTerm 1
